#: includes/settings-page.php:460
msgid "Settings on this screen that apply only to the comment form and the REST API comments endpoint. Thresholds shared with every other guarded form (Login, CF7, WooCommerce, and the rest) live in Timing & Token Engine below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:466
msgid "Enable Init Void Shield"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:472
msgid "Activate the honeypot defense on comment forms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:480
msgid "Apply to Logged-in Users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:486
msgid "Also verify comments from logged-in users."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:489
msgid "By default, logged-in users are trusted and bypass all checks. Enable this if your site has open registration or untrusted members."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:497
msgid "Block REST API Comments"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:503
msgid "Reject comments submitted directly through the REST API (wp/v2/comments)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:506
msgid "The honeypot and JS token checks above only cover the classic comment form; REST API submissions bypass them entirely. Enable this only if your site does not rely on a headless app or other legitimate client that posts comments via the REST API."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:514
msgid "Require Same-Site Referer"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:520
msgid "Reject a comment submission whose Referer header is missing or points to a different site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:523
msgid "Catches a scripted bot that posts directly to the comment endpoint without ever loading the page. Off by default: some privacy-focused browsers and extensions strip the Referer header even on a real, same-site submission, which this cannot tell apart from a bot. Enable only after confirming it does not affect real visitors on your site, and use it alongside the other layers, not instead of them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:529
msgid "Timing & Token Engine"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:531
msgid "These thresholds are shared by the core engine: comments, the WordPress core forms below, and every form plugin integration on this page all use them, not comments alone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:537
msgid "Minimum Submit Time"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:546
#: includes/settings-page.php:565
#: includes/settings-page.php:603
msgid "seconds"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:548
msgid "Comments and other content-style forms (topics, replies, contact forms) submitted faster than this will be rejected. Humans need time to read and type. Login, registration, and other account forms use the separate setting below instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:556
msgid "Account Forms Minimum Submit Time"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:567
msgid "Separate, shorter floor used by the Login, Registration, Lost Password, Multisite Signup, WooCommerce registration, and BuddyPress registration guards instead of the general Minimum Submit Time above. A browser autofilling a saved username and password lets a genuine visitor submit far faster than someone typing a comment from scratch, so these forms need a lower bar. Set to 0 to disable this specific check for account forms while keeping every other layer (honeypot fields, JS/headless detection, signed time token) fully active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:575
msgid "JavaScript Token Delay"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:584
msgid "milliseconds"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:586
msgid "Delay before the hidden JS token is injected. Catches headless browsers that submit instantly. A small random amount of extra time is always added on top of this value so the exact wait cannot be read from the page source and timed around."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:594
msgid "Maximum Token Age"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:605
msgid "A submission carrying a token older than this is rejected, so a token cannot be captured once and replayed indefinitely. On a site with full-page caching, a token is baked in at the moment a page is cached, not the moment a visitor actually loads it — if comments from real visitors are being rejected as expired, raise this to comfortably cover your cache lifetime, or enable Lazy Fetch below instead of raising it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:611
msgid "WordPress Core Forms"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:613
msgid "Optional honeypot protection for the default WordPress login, registration, and lost-password forms at wp-login.php. Disabled by default, since these guard authentication itself — review your setup after enabling."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:619
msgid "Guard Login Form"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:625
msgid "Protect the default WP login form against automated login attempts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:633
msgid "Login Guard Scope"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:638
msgid "Everywhere (wp-login.php + any front-end wp_login_form() usage)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:639
msgid "wp-login.php only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:642
msgid "If your theme or a plugin renders a login form on the front end with wp_login_form() (e.g. a login page, widget, or modal) and that page may be served by a full-page cache, choose \"wp-login.php only\" to leave that specific form unguarded rather than risk real visitors being rejected. This uses the Referer header as a heuristic to tell the two forms apart, which a determined bot could spoof — the default (\"Everywhere\") gives the strongest protection and is recommended unless you hit this specific situation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:650
msgid "Guard Registration Form"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:656
msgid "Protect the default WP registration form (wp-login.php?action=register)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:659
msgid "Only applies if user registration is open. Multisite signup (wp-signup.php) uses a different form and is not covered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:667
msgid "Guard Lost Password Form"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:673
msgid "Protect the default WP lost-password form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:681
msgid "Guard Multisite Signup Form"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:687
msgid "Protect the site/user signup form at wp-signup.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:692
msgid "Multisite detected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:694
msgid "This site is not a Multisite network; this guard has no effect here."
msgstr ""

