#: includes/settings-page.php:753
msgid "Community & E-commerce Integrations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:755
msgid "Optional honeypot protection for WooCommerce, bbPress, and BuddyPress. Each toggle only takes effect if the corresponding plugin is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:761
msgid "WooCommerce Registration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:767
msgid "Add the honeypot guard to the WooCommerce \"My Account\" registration form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:776
msgid "bbPress Topics & Replies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:782
msgid "Add the honeypot guard to the New Topic and Reply forms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:791
msgid "BuddyPress Registration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:797
msgid "Add the honeypot guard to the BuddyPress signup form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:804
msgid "Advanced Protection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:809
msgid "Custom Field Prefix"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:819
msgid "Prefix used to build the hidden honeypot field names (lowercase letters, numbers, underscore only). Change this if you suspect a spammer has targeted your site specifically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:827
msgid "CSS Trap Rotation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:833
msgid "Randomize the CSS technique and field order used to hide honeypot traps on every render."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:836
msgid "Makes it harder for CSS-aware bots to learn a single fixed pattern. Traps remain invisible to humans either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:844
msgid "Headless Browser Detection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:850
msgid "Flag common automation signals (navigator.webdriver, zero-size browser window) picked up by the JS token script."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:853
msgid "Lightweight, client-side only, no external calls. Disable this if you use browser-automation tools to test submissions on your own site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:861
msgid "Block Non-Browser User Agents"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:867
msgid "Reject submissions whose User-Agent header identifies a known scripted HTTP client (curl, Python requests, Go, Scrapy, and similar)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:870
msgid "A real browser running the JS layer always sends its own browser User-Agent, so a match here is a near-zero-false-positive signal. Catches a bot that never runs JavaScript at all and simply replays the static form fields, which the honeypot and JS checks alone cannot see. On by default; the list of signatures is filterable for developers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:878
msgid "Require Real User Interaction"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:884
msgid "Also require at least one real mouse, keyboard, touch, or scroll event before the form is accepted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:887
msgid "Catches bots that simply wait out the JavaScript Token Delay instead of interacting with the page. An interaction is only counted after a short minimum delay of its own, so a bot cannot satisfy this by firing one synthetic event the instant the page loads. Off by default; works best with a JavaScript Token Delay of at least 1-2 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:895
msgid "Lazy Fetch (Cache-Safe Tokens)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:901
msgid "Refresh the time token via a small same-origin JavaScript request as soon as the page truly loads, instead of relying only on the value baked in when the page was rendered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings-page.php:904
msgid "Recommended for sites with aggressive full-page caching. On such a site, the token baked into a cached page reflects the moment the page was cached, not the moment a real visitor loaded it, which can make legitimate comments look expired under a low Maximum Token Age. When enabled, this refreshes the token client-side (plain JavaScript, no jQuery) right after the page loads, so timing is always measured from the real visit — applies to every guarded form, not just comments. If the request fails or JavaScript is unavailable, the original baked-in token is used as a fallback, so this can only help. Off by default."
msgstr ""

